# Slice 3 · FastAPI Backend + One Real AI Workflow

*Stop mocking · one document type · end-to-end real*

---

## Why

Mocks prove the UX. This slice proves the AI.
Pick the easiest path: PDF supplier invoice → text → classify → summarize → extract → display.
Everything else (Ask My Company, Draft Reply) stays mocked until this proves out.

---

## Scope (sketch — refine when slice-2 lands)

```
infra      docker-compose: postgres + pgvector
           restructure repo: apps/web + apps/api + infra/

api        FastAPI scaffold
           endpoints: workspace · document · analysis · audit
           SQLAlchemy models per technical_stack §5 data model
           Alembic migrations

ingest     PDF upload · text extraction (text-PDF only · no OCR yet)
           background task for analysis (FastAPI BackgroundTasks for now)

ai         provider adapter (start: ONE provider — Mistral or OpenAI-compatible)
           runtime prompts: classifier v1 · summary v1 · invoice-extractor v1
           embed version line inside each prompt template
                # prompt: <name> v<version>
           validate JSON output against Pydantic schemas
           save prompt_runs records per registry §23.5

ui         /app/inbox switches from static JSON to API
           upload UI · loading states · empty/error states
           keep slice-2 mocks for Ask My Company and Draft Reply

acceptance  upload one of the 5 invoice PDFs from §23.3
            card appears in inbox within ~10s
            extracted fields match the "Expected extraction" block (high accuracy on
              supplier_name · invoice_number · total_amount · due_date)
            audit event logged · no hallucinated amounts · missing fields surfaced honestly
```

